{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c8660606-1ad9-4649-853a-3db355b31bac","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9685c43475d66d54","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-esud_d8x/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Resolve structured log field convention scope\n\n## Description\n\nResolves whether the structured reconciliation-log field convention for rhods-operator includes fields beyond `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` (for example, reconciliation attempt count or error category). The strategy's required fields are `name`/`namespace` (P0) and `resourceKind` (P0 for controllers whose kind is not implied by their name, P1 elsewhere); this open question — owned by PM and the Observability team per the strategy — must be decided before the codebase-wide conversion begins, so that every log call site is touched exactly once with the final field set. This is a decision-type investigation: the outcome selects the field set that the manager-binary conversion, the cloudmanager-binary conversion, and the convention documentation all apply.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Confirm the required field set for reconciliation error logs: `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`, using camelCase key names per controller-runtime convention.\n- Decide whether to include additional fields (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category), explicitly weighing query utility against log-volume growth.\n- Record the decision with rationale and communicate it to the conversion and documentation workstreams so a single final field set is applied.\n- Bounded outcomes: (a) minimal three-field convention; (b) extended field set. Both outcomes keep the same downstream work structure — only the field set applied at each call site changes — so the conditionality is recorded as a rewrite gate on the downstream work rather than as separate conditional plans.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The field-set decision is recorded: required fields confirmed, and additional fields explicitly included or excluded, with the utility-versus-log-volume rationale documented.\n- The decision is confirmed with the PM / Observability stakeholders who own the open question in the strategy.\n- The recorded outcome is sufficient for the conversion work to apply the final field set in a single pass, with no field-set changes after conversion begins.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables HLR1-HLR7 (determines the exact field set the conversions apply at every call site); no HLR is directly satisfied by this epic. Resolves the strategy's open question on convention field scope, which gates the conversion and documentation work.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":86348,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3185ffb52f6b41f","agent_id":"a48435a52b6e40103","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"0f9dd2d0-81b4-4d53-a524-8570fc6f3c70","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:23:36.136Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
