{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-cfc1ffb6-74ae-4034-9879-74bf2dc52b2d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab374e2a5f9319fa","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-esud_d8x/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E003.md","content":"# Convert cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs to structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nApplies the structured resource-context conversion to the cloudmanager binary's multi-cloud infrastructure controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine). These controllers are built on the same controller-runtime/logr foundation and use the shared reconciler pattern, so they already receive `name`/`namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger; the work converts any message-embedded resource identity in reconciliation error paths to structured key-value pairs and adds `resourceKind`, applying the field set confirmed by the structured log field convention scope decision. This epic is independently schedulable from the manager-binary conversion: it is a separate binary, deployed only on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave), so its impact scope is narrower than the manager binary.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit `log.Error()` call sites in cloudmanager reconciliation error paths.\n- Convert call sites that embed resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value pairs per the resolved convention field set.\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all three cloudmanager controllers' reconciliation error logs (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine).\n- Risks and notes: whether the cloudmanager conversion ships in the same release as the manager-binary conversion or in a subsequent release is an open PM scheduling decision — this epic is independently schedulable, blocks no manager-binary work, and its timing follows that release decision. The consolidated log-consumer validation covers the cloudmanager portion when this conversion lands.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Unit tests assert that cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs contain `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields with correct values.\n- No `log.Error` call in a cloudmanager reconciliation error path embeds resource name or namespace in message text — verified by the CI lint/static-analysis rule introduced with the convention enforcement, passing with zero violations on the cloudmanager code.\n- A before/after log output comparison for a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error shows the structured fields present in the new format.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR1 [P0] — reconciliation error logs embedding name/namespace in message strings converted to structured KV pairs (cloudmanager-binary portion).\n- HLR5 [P0] — cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88347,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3185ffb52f6b41f","agent_id":"a48435a52b6e40103","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"8f9c1a7b-1ae3-44c6-99ee-ad425ebf9913","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:24:00.440Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
