{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-dff89dd9-c13d-49b7-ad3a-5a185ab2f704","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aae6850a30348e20","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-esud_d8x/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E004.md","content":"# Validate log consumer compatibility and audit alert-rule impact\n\n## Description\n\nConsolidated pre-merge validation that resolves the strategy's open question of which existing log-based alerts and dashboards rely on message-string patterns that will change when resource identity moves from log message text into structured key-value pairs. Deploys a test build carrying the converted log format to a dev cluster configured with the production log consumer stack, triggers reconciliation errors in both operator binaries, and verifies ingestion and alert-query behavior for the old and new formats (Loki on OpenShift; CloudWatch on cloud deployments). The strategy requires this identification before the converted format merges.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Deploy a test build with the converted log format to a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack configured; trigger sample reconciliation errors in the manager and cloudmanager binaries.\n- Perform the before/after log output comparison for sample reconciliation errors: confirm structured fields appear and log consumers (Loki, CloudWatch) ingest both formats without configuration changes.\n- With SRE/Support coordination, inventory existing text-based alert rules and log-based dashboards that rely on message-string patterns that change; identify owners and a disposition for each (query still matches, or remediation needed).\n- Produce the validation report: ingestion evidence, the alert-rule inventory with dispositions, and remediation items for SRE-owned rules.\n- Risks and notes: dev-cluster and production-log-consumer-stack availability is an environment precondition — this epic's work includes standing up the configuration where possible, but access granted by other parties is not controlled here. Updates to SRE-owned alert rules may fall outside this strategy's delivery scope (the strategy excludes custom dashboards and alerting rules); remediation items are handed off with owners. If the cloudmanager release-timing decision defers that conversion, the cloudmanager portion of this validation re-runs when it lands.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The validation report shows, with before/after evidence for sample reconciliation errors, that structured fields appear and the production log consumer stack (Loki, CloudWatch) ingests both the old and new formats without configuration changes.\n- The inventory of message-string-dependent alert rules and dashboards is complete, confirmed with SRE/Support, and every affected rule has a recorded disposition (still matches, or remediation item with owner).\n- The report is delivered in time to gate the merge of the converted log format, per the strategy's before-merge requirement.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- No HLR is directly satisfied by this epic. It verifies the backwards-compatibility non-functional requirement covering the HLR1-HLR6 deliverables (log ingestion pipelines must not break; text-based alert rules identified and coordinated), and resolves the strategy's open question on affected log-based alerts/dashboards.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":89062,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3185ffb52f6b41f","agent_id":"a48435a52b6e40103","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"df812e87-4df4-4d4d-83f1-f9e7fa5cbc91","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:24:10.361Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
