mples, DSCI key migration guide) — folded into this guideline rather than duplicated.\n- **Publication for external operator adoption**: publish the convention as a specification for voluntary adoption and file tracking issues in the COO projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator). External adoption itself is best-effort and not a completion condition.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The contribution guideline exists and specifies the required fields, the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis with before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented conversions — the field list and code examples match the shipped manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary logging.\n- The DSCI key-migration guide provides before/after query examples and is included in the release-notes documentation of the migration.\n- The convention is published for external operator adoption and tracking issues are filed in the COO projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator); voluntary adoption by those teams is explicitly out of scope.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR8 [P1] — document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":89814,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3185ffb52f6b41f","agent_id":"a48435a52b6e40103","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"4b83ce56-3f92-4dc4-b233-ab3ede72ac2e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:24:19.995Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
