{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5918d0c33be9d03","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Convert manager binary reconciliation error logs to structured resource context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the convention-scope decision adopts fields beyond name/namespace/resourceKind\n15\t    (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category), apply the extended field\n16\t    set at the same call sites - the conversion pattern is rewritten, not the epic\n17\t    structure.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Convert manager binary reconciliation error logs to structured resource context\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConverts all reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator manager binary from message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` — camelCase per controller-runtime convention), applying the field set confirmed by the structured log field convention scope decision. The work spans all five controller tiers of the manager binary and all 15 action files across four tiers, and includes migrating the DSCInitialization controller from its non-standard key names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) to the standard convention. It also introduces the CI lint rule that enforces the convention for future controller development.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in manager-binary reconciliation error paths and track coverage in a checklist. This audit also confirms the actual share of call sites embedding resource identity (Staff Engineer input reports ~75%) — the conversion proceeds over every embedded call site regardless of the percentage.\n44\t- Convert every call site that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value pairs, applying the resolved convention field set (e.g., `log.Error(err, \"reconciliation failed\", \"name\", obj.Name, \"namespace\", obj.Namespace, \"resourceKind\", \"Dashboard\")`).\n45\t- Add `resourceKind` to reconciliation error logs across all controller tiers:\n46\t  - DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller and the 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI) — the P1 queryability enhancement is bundled into the same call-site edits as the P0 identity conversion.\n47\t  - Module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator).\n48\t  - DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller.\n49\t  - 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — kind is not implied by controller name for these.\n50\t- Migrate DSCI structured keys from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace`.\n51\t- Cover all 15 action files across 4 tiers: 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n52\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — never a spurious namespace value.\n53\t- Add a CI lint/static-analysis rule flagging `log.Error` calls that embed name/namespace in message text or omit the required structured fields.\n54\t- Risks and notes: the DSCI key migration must land in a single release to avoid long-term inconsistency, and operators with existing queries on the old key names are supported by the migration guide documented in the convention documentation workstream; SRE/Support coordination on affected alert rules is handled by the consolidated log-consumer validation workstream. Effort note: the audit-plus-conversion is estimated at ~1.25-1.5 sprints as one mechanical pass over one surface; re-split by controller tier if the call-site audit reveals materially more embedded-identity call sites than the ~75% estimate implies.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- The CI lint/static-analysis rule passes with zero violations on the manager binary: no `log.Error` call in a reconciliation error path embeds resource name or namespace in message text, and required structured fields are present.\n59\t- Unit tests assert that reconciliation error logs across all five controller tiers and all 15 action files contain `name`, `namespace` (where the resource is namespaced), and `resourceKind` with correct values.\n60\t- DSCI reconciliation error logs use the standard camelCase field names, and a codebase grep confirms no remaining references to `Request.Name` or `DSCInitialization` as structured log keys.\n61\t- Cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) emit `name` and `resourceKind` with `namespace` omitted or empty — unit tests confirm no spurious namespace value.\n62\t- The call-site audit checklist is complete, covering every `log.Error` call site in manager-binary reconciliation error paths.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR1 [P0] — reconciliation error logs embedding name/namespace in message strings converted to structured KV pairs (manager-binary portion).\n67\t- HLR2 [P0] — DSCI controller migrated from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to camelCase convention.\n68\t- HLR3 [P0] — service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) error logs include `resourceKind`.\n69\t- HLR4 [P0] — action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module action files).\n70\t- HLR6 [P0] — module controller error logs (8 module handlers) include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`.\n71\t- HLR7 [P1] — DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` (bundled: added in the same edit at the same call sites as the HLR1 identity conversion; not separately schedulable without double-touching every call site).\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbd21d00a17c8887","agent_id":"a75f8bdcfb2bb8afa","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"1d9c502e-1afc-4747-9a32-a45666b08b6b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:26:40.475Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5918d0c33be9d03","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
