{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-860af89a352af950","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: Convert cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs to structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the convention-scope decision adopts fields beyond name/namespace/resourceKind,\n16\t    apply the extended field set at the same cloudmanager call sites - the conversion\n17\t    pattern is rewritten, not the epic structure.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Convert cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs to structured resource context\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tApplies the structured resource-context conversion to the cloudmanager binary's multi-cloud infrastructure controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine). These controllers are built on the same controller-runtime/logr foundation and use the shared reconciler pattern, so they already receive `name`/`namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger; the work converts any message-embedded resource identity in reconciliation error paths to structured key-value pairs and adds `resourceKind`, applying the field set confirmed by the structured log field convention scope decision. This epic is independently schedulable from the manager-binary conversion: it is a separate binary, deployed only on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave), so its impact scope is narrower than the manager binary.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Audit `log.Error()` call sites in cloudmanager reconciliation error paths.\n44\t- Convert call sites that embed resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value pairs per the resolved convention field set.\n45\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all three cloudmanager controllers' reconciliation error logs (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine).\n46\t- Risks and notes: whether the cloudmanager conversion ships in the same release as the manager-binary conversion or in a subsequent release is an open PM scheduling decision — this epic is independently schedulable, blocks no manager-binary work, and its timing follows that release decision. The consolidated log-consumer validation covers the cloudmanager portion when this conversion lands.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Unit tests assert that cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs contain `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields with correct values.\n51\t- No `log.Error` call in a cloudmanager reconciliation error path embeds resource name or namespace in message text — verified by the CI lint/static-analysis rule introduced with the convention enforcement, passing with zero violations on the cloudmanager code.\n52\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error shows the structured fields present in the new format.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR1 [P0] — reconciliation error logs embedding name/namespace in message strings converted to structured KV pairs (cloudmanager-binary portion).\n57\t- HLR5 [P0] — cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbd21d00a17c8887","agent_id":"a75f8bdcfb2bb8afa","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"d8fad3e0-5968-43aa-a92b-29f8c3aadff6","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:26:43.894Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-860af89a352af950","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
