{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89125d61b77cd3c4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E004\n3\ttitle: Validate log consumer compatibility and audit alert-rule impact\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n12\tinvestigation_signals:\n13\t  question_specificity: 1\n14\t  source_accessibility: 0\n15\t  local_runnability: 0\n16\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n17\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n18\timplementation_type: null\n19\tai_signals: null\n20\tai_implementability: Low\n21\tai_implementability_score: -2\n22\tjira_key: null\n23\tbranch: null\n24\tgated_by: null\n25\tgate_failure_impact: null\n26\t---\n27\t# Validate log consumer compatibility and audit alert-rule impact\n28\t\n29\t## Description\n30\t\n31\tConsolidated pre-merge validation that resolves the strategy's open question of which existing log-based alerts and dashboards rely on message-string patterns that will change when resource identity moves from log message text into structured key-value pairs. Deploys a test build carrying the converted log format to a dev cluster configured with the production log consumer stack, triggers reconciliation errors in both operator binaries, and verifies ingestion and alert-query behavior for the old and new formats (Loki on OpenShift; CloudWatch on cloud deployments). The strategy requires this identification before the converted format merges.\n32\t\n33\t## Scope\n34\t\n35\t- Deploy a test build with the converted log format to a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack configured; trigger sample reconciliation errors in the manager and cloudmanager binaries.\n36\t- Perform the before/after log output comparison for sample reconciliation errors: confirm structured fields appear and log consumers (Loki, CloudWatch) ingest both formats without configuration changes.\n37\t- With SRE/Support coordination, inventory existing text-based alert rules and log-based dashboards that rely on message-string patterns that change; identify owners and a disposition for each (query still matches, or remediation needed).\n38\t- Produce the validation report: ingestion evidence, the alert-rule inventory with dispositions, and remediation items for SRE-owned rules.\n39\t- Risks and notes: dev-cluster and production-log-consumer-stack availability is an environment precondition — this epic's work includes standing up the configuration where possible, but access granted by other parties is not controlled here. Updates to SRE-owned alert rules may fall outside this strategy's delivery scope (the strategy excludes custom dashboards and alerting rules); remediation items are handed off with owners. If the cloudmanager release-timing decision defers that conversion, the cloudmanager portion of this validation re-runs when it lands.\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- The validation report shows, with before/after evidence for sample reconciliation errors, that structured fields appear and the production log consumer stack (Loki, CloudWatch) ingests both the old and new formats without configuration changes.\n44\t- The inventory of message-string-dependent alert rules and dashboards is complete, confirmed with SRE/Support, and every affected rule has a recorded disposition (still matches, or remediation item with owner).\n45\t- The report is delivered in time to gate the merge of the converted log format, per the strategy's before-merge requirement.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- No HLR is directly satisfied by this epic. It verifies the backwards-compatibility non-functional requirement covering the HLR1-HLR6 deliverables (log ingestion pipelines must not break; text-based alert rules identified and coordinated), and resolves the strategy's open question on affected log-based alerts/dashboards.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbd21d00a17c8887","agent_id":"a75f8bdcfb2bb8afa","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"8e505376-dbd9-4d48-b271-f54ce76318da","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:26:44.504Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89125d61b77cd3c4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
