{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90372b28c73f2fc6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E005\n3\ttitle: Document and publish the structured log convention\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E004\n15\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n16\tgate_failure_impact:\n17\t  action: rewrite\n18\t  fallback_approach: If the resolved convention includes fields beyond name/namespace/resourceKind,\n19\t    the guideline documents the extended field set; if kept minimal, it documents\n20\t    the three-field convention as specified.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: -1\n27\t  external_dependency: 0\n28\t  human_process_gates: -1\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: Medium\n33\tai_implementability_score: 2\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Document and publish the structured log convention\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tAuthors the contribution guideline documenting the structured log field convention for rhods-operator controller development, and publishes the convention for external operator adoption — the Cluster Observability Operator components (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) adopt it at their discretion per platform policy overlay 0008 (RHOAI does not install, manage, or control external operator dependencies). Includes the DSCI key-migration guide with before/after query examples and the release-notes documentation of the migration. Runs last: the documentation describes what was built and is finalized from the log-consumer validation results.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\tContent outline:\n46\t\n47\t- **Contribution guideline** for new controller development, specifying:\n48\t  - Required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` — plus any additional fields adopted by the convention field-scope decision), with camelCase key naming rationale per controller-runtime convention.\n49\t  - The three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded resource identity, non-standard DSCI key names (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and missing `resourceKind`.\n50\t  - Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n51\t- **DSCI key-name migration guide**: release-notes documentation with before/after query examples for operators using `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`-based Loki/CloudWatch queries, noting the single-release transition.\n52\t- **Design doc content** committed by the strategy (three-problem diagnosis, before/after code examples, DSCI key migration guide) — folded into this guideline rather than duplicated.\n53\t- **Publication for external operator adoption**: publish the convention as a specification for voluntary adoption and file tracking issues in the COO projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator). External adoption itself is best-effort and not a completion condition.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The contribution guideline exists and specifies the required fields, the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis with before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n58\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented conversions — the field list and code examples match the shipped manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary logging.\n59\t- The DSCI key-migration guide provides before/after query examples and is included in the release-notes documentation of the migration.\n60\t- The convention is published for external operator adoption and tracking issues are filed in the COO projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator); voluntary adoption by those teams is explicitly out of scope.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR8 [P1] — document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbd21d00a17c8887","agent_id":"a75f8bdcfb2bb8afa","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"91190184-11d6-4815-b348-f74c3a419683","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:26:45.103Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-90372b28c73f2fc6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
