ation results.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\tContent outline:\n46\t\n47\t- **Contribution guideline** for new controller development, specifying:\n48\t  - Required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` — plus any additional fields adopted by the convention field-scope decision), with camelCase key naming rationale per controller-runtime convention.\n49\t  - The three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded resource identity, non-standard DSCI key names (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and missing `resourceKind`.\n50\t  - Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n51\t- **DSCI key-name migration guide**: release-notes documentation with before/after query examples for operators using `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`-based Loki/CloudWatch queries, noting the single-release transition.\n52\t- **Design doc content** committed by the strategy (three-problem diagnosis, before/after code examples, DSCI key migration guide) — folded into this guideline rather than duplicated.\n53\t- **Publication for external operator adoption**: publish the convention as a specification for voluntary adoption and file tracking issues in the COO projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator). External adoption itself is best-effort and not a completion condition.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The contribution guideline exists and specifies the required fields, the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis with before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n58\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented conversions — the field list and code examples match the shipped manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary logging.\n59\t- The DSCI key-migration guide provides before/after query examples and is included in the release-notes documentation of the migration.\n60\t- The convention is published for external operator adoption and tracking issues are filed in the COO projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator); voluntary adoption by those teams is explicitly out of scope.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR8 [P1] — document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c461daf22144665","agent_id":"aaac70143c66c04c1","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"b782bd3d-f10b-4214-be5a-402f17f9a344","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:34:07.439Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b08d0abeb065f823","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
