{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b52b1caca2d11744","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Resolve structured log field convention scope\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Resolve structured log field convention scope\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves whether the structured reconciliation-log field convention for rhods-operator includes fields beyond `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` (for example, reconciliation attempt count or error category). The strategy's required fields are `name`/`namespace` (P0) and `resourceKind` (P0 for controllers whose kind is not implied by their name, P1 elsewhere); this open question — owned by PM and the Observability team per the strategy — must be decided before the codebase-wide conversion begins, so that every log call site is touched exactly once with the final field set. This is a decision-type investigation: the outcome selects the field set that the manager-binary conversion, the cloudmanager-binary conversion, and the convention documentation all apply.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Confirm the required field set for reconciliation error logs: `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`, using camelCase key names per controller-runtime convention.\n34\t- Decide whether to include additional fields (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category), explicitly weighing query utility against log-volume growth.\n35\t- Record the decision with rationale and communicate it to the conversion and documentation workstreams so a single final field set is applied.\n36\t- Bounded outcomes: (a) minimal three-field convention; (b) extended field set. Both outcomes keep the same downstream work structure — only the field set applied at each call site changes — so the conditionality is recorded as a rewrite gate on the downstream work rather than as separate conditional plans.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- The field-set decision is recorded: required fields confirmed, and additional fields explicitly included or excluded, with the utility-versus-log-volume rationale documented.\n41\t- The decision is confirmed with the PM / Observability stakeholders who own the open question in the strategy.\n42\t- The recorded outcome is sufficient for the conversion work to apply the final field set in a single pass, with no field-set changes after conversion begins.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- Enables HLR1-HLR7 (determines the exact field set the conversions apply at every call site); no HLR is directly satisfied by this epic. Resolves the strategy's open question on convention field scope, which gates the conversion and documentation work.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-85a9d24aa1f36caa","agent_id":"a17e4293d1382f64b","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"4a8f43ec-aaaf-4d90-b967-bb2e7e06de22","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:35:20.407Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b52b1caca2d11744","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
