ences (`E00N`) appear in any epic body — cross-epic references consistently use descriptive workstream phrasing.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nFull scope coverage: all five manager-binary controller tiers, the 15 action files across 4 tiers (SME-corrected counts), DSCI key migration, cluster-scoped-resource handling, the CI lint rule, the cloudmanager controllers, the contribution guideline, DSCI migration guide with before/after query examples, release-notes documentation, design-doc content (folded into E005 rather than duplicated), and external publication with COO tracking issues. All seven strategy ACs map to epic ACs. All four open questions are explicitly dispositioned (two as Investigations, one as a PM scheduling decision recorded as a health warning, one as informational audit work baked into E002's scope) plus the SME-resolved question. Strategy-level risks are carried forward (DSCI query breakage → single-release note in E002 + migration guide in E005; log-consumer regression → E004; adoption delay → E005). A docs-authoring epic exists (HLR8 requires documentation regardless of the \"Pending human review\" process-gate boilerplate). No conditional branch files were generated, and the no-branch decision is justified: E001's bounded outcomes change only the field set, not epic structure — recorded as rewrite gates on E002/E003/E005.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46300,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-85a9d24aa1f36caa","agent_id":"a17e4293d1382f64b","session_id":"5fd65945-afc1-4d94-9de3-0f90915cbf9f","uuid":"7cc6e324-87e6-48a1-8a45-d6e45fb990d3","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:38:49.784Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
